## UAE Civil Transactions Law (Federal Law No. 5 of 1985), Article 390 —
## Liquidated damages cap
##
## Source: Federal Law No. 5 of 1985 (UAE), Article 390(2). Where the
## parties have agreed an amount of compensation in advance (a
## "liquidated damages" / "agreed compensation" clause), the court may
## reduce the amount if the obligor proves that the agreed sum is
## *grossly exaggerated* relative to the actual loss, *or* increase it
## if grossly inadequate. ADGM CFI applies this article to commercial
## contracts governed by UAE law (sometimes alongside the federal cap
## doctrine in case-law).
##
## Used in:
##   trace-04 — ADGMCFI-2024-320 Projeco v Ideacrate.
##
## The 10% cap convention applied in trace-04 reflects ADGM CFI's
## case-law treatment of the "grossly exaggerated" limb in standard
## commercial-contract LD clauses; the *cap rate* is a parameter,
## not a universal of Article 390 itself.

```catala
declaration structure LDClaim:
  data uncapped_amount_aed content decimal
  data contract_value_aed content decimal
  data cap_rate content decimal
  ## The court must have determined that the agreed sum is grossly
  ## exaggerated relative to the actual loss before the cap engages.
  ## This is a human-judgment input, not a deterministic predicate.
  data court_finds_grossly_exaggerated content boolean

declaration structure LDAward:
  data cap_aed content decimal
  data awarded_aed content decimal
  data was_capped content boolean

declaration scope Article390Cap:
  input claim content LDClaim
  output award content LDAward

scope Article390Cap:
  definition award equals
    let cap equals claim.contract_value_aed * claim.cap_rate in
    let awarded equals
      if claim.court_finds_grossly_exaggerated then
        (if claim.uncapped_amount_aed > cap then cap
         else claim.uncapped_amount_aed)
      else claim.uncapped_amount_aed
    in
    LDAward {
      -- cap_aed: cap
      -- awarded_aed: awarded
      -- was_capped: awarded < claim.uncapped_amount_aed
    }
```

## Test — replays the 10% cap from trace-04.

```catala
#[test] declaration scope TestArt390CapEngages:
  composite scope Article390Cap
  output award content LDAward

scope TestArt390CapEngages:
  definition award equals composite.award
  ## trace-04: contract value AED 6,085,211.90; uncapped LDs AED
  ## 9,700,000. Court applied 10% cap → AED 608,521.19. The court
  ## made the "grossly exaggerated" finding, so the cap engages.
  definition composite.claim equals
    LDClaim {
      -- uncapped_amount_aed: 9700000.00
      -- contract_value_aed: 6085211.90
      -- cap_rate: 0.10
      -- court_finds_grossly_exaggerated: true
    }
  assertion award.cap_aed = 608521.19
  assertion award.awarded_aed = 608521.19
  assertion award.was_capped = true

#[test] declaration scope TestArt390NoExaggerationFinding:
  composite scope Article390Cap
  output award content LDAward

scope TestArt390NoExaggerationFinding:
  definition award equals composite.award
  ## If the court does not find the LD grossly exaggerated, Article
  ## 390(2) does not engage and the agreed sum stands.
  definition composite.claim equals
    LDClaim {
      -- uncapped_amount_aed: 50000.00
      -- contract_value_aed: 1000000.00
      -- cap_rate: 0.10
      -- court_finds_grossly_exaggerated: false
    }
  assertion award.awarded_aed = 50000.00
  assertion award.was_capped = false
```
